My second ever UnNethack ascension, notable in that I managed to keep
Polyselfless Genoless Elberethless conduct.  Only the latter two were
intentional.

On the whole I was very, very lucky with early equipment and with
intrinsics, getting the whole set from a minimum number of monsters.
Also had more than my fair share of altars and temples.  Lots of
temples + early pet dragon = loads of spellbooks! :-)  There were very
few things I didn't find in this game, but most noticably I never had
any unholy water, "oReflection or magical instruments.

Dumplog is here:
http://un.nethack.nu/users/spontiff/dumps/spontiff.1285711762.txt.html

66600 turns of ttyrecs are there if anyone really wants to put
themselves through watching it!

Highlights include:

having to dive down after my kitten who fell through a trapdoor on
DL1.  I ended up a level deeper than him, but near the upstair, and
found him again fairly quick.

Two altars on DL1 (both cross-aligned, but I converted them and set up
stash there.)

k with a /oMM in minetown, but my healing spell saved me until he ran
out of charges.  I had fallen into minetown, so my 72HP cat wasn't
with me.  I tamed a second kitten and buffed it up on easy monsters
(including that kobold).

Got a magic lamp (used as a light source), can of grease and towel
from the various minetown stores and lev boots, speed boots, HoB,
silver saber and CoMR from a handy armoury in the main dungeon.

Went just under 7k turns before I broke pacifist conduct for a sac
victim to see if I could make holy water safely (wasn't intending to
do a pacifist run, but was keeping my pre-protection XP for a
potential floating eye).  It didn't drop a corpse...

Read a scroll of charming when I found a magic whistle and a baby
dragon in the SokoZoo and ended up with a pet chameleon, which was fun
for a while!

Double sokoprize: there was a /oDeath inside the BoH (the other
choices were "oESP and CoMR, which I already had).

Polytrap dance at Mines' End turned my cat, Hertmes, into a Sirrush,
who took care of a load of shopkeepers and temple priests for me,
giving me magic missile, restore ability, identify and more.
I lost this pet later on, only to find out that it'd discovered the
quest portal and was hanging out with all the other Ds.  Feral,
unfortunately, but he did drop acid scales for me when I let my
current pet (a vampire from more polytrap fun) take care of him.

Left my vampire lord taking his time over a dragon corpse on Home 2 to
BUC-test some potions upstairs, came back down and a guivre
immediately disintegrated my shield.  Left the V down there to fend
for himself and went off to find a source of reflection.

Had enough cash left after having bought 9 points of protection at XL2
to buy(!!) everything I wanted from One-Eyed Sam, who appeared above
Medusa's level.  Mainly a second lamp that I turned into reflecting
scales, and some much needed enchant weapon scrolls. After that the
quest was easy, cyclops fell to the /oDeath.  The V was still tame and
I made a second set of reflecting scale mail for him.

Prime lesson learnt: don't give your pet vampire reflecting DSM unless
you really don't need it any more - he sucked on a doppleganger
corpse, turned into a wyvern, and promptly ate the drained corpse only
to turn into a shrieker.

Castle wand (1:1) went on two markers, mainly to up my AC, provide
remove curse scrolls and recharge wands of death.

Asmodeus' level provided a handy little swarm of cockatrices, although
the foocubi alongside them did make me a little nervous of wielding c
corpses recklessly.

Tamed a cat in Baalzebub's lair and bashed it over the head with a !
oPoly - I got a vorpal jabberwock, but it found a polytrap
depressingly soon after and became a horse.  I managed to turn it into
a dragon of some kind for a while, but it turned into a fire ant soon
after, then a python, and got smushed by a minotaur in Orcus Town.

Had a bit of trouble with purple Ls summonstorming, but it tended to
happen on the maze levels, where it's not such a big deal.  Between
the saber, the Staff, magic missile and the occasional volley of
daggers, I had plenty in my arsenal to deal with it, and my -34AC kept
me from losing health too much.  A lich dropped an athame, but I'd
come this far without the E word so I just kept it for emergencies.

Found the vibrating square, went back for Rodney, ran down to perform
the invocation and headed into the sanctum.  That's where things got a
bit hairy.  Rodney came back as soon as I arrived, and lay in wait in
duplicate ('Double Trouble!') beside Cthulhu.  Getting over the
drawbridges was fine (I even picked up a !oGL of unknown beatitude
that I was hoping might be my ticket out of the sanctum), but then I
realised I was straining to recall all my healing spells and magic
missile.  Oh dear.  The combination of L, h, &, D and priests were a
tough slog to get through, but eventually a zap from my SDD revealed
the door to where the real bad guys lurked.

I'd kept an uncursed chickatrice figurine I'd found in the Town branch
for the sanctum, took it out, used it (luckily it wasn't tame), and
slaughtered it.  Then Cthulhu (basically a master master mindflayer
who has the Amulet in UnNethack) picked the square it'd dropped a
corpse on as the place he was going to stand, and just wouldn't move!
Luckily a guivre disintegrated one Rodney, and my /oDeath took care of
the other while I waited for the damn h to get off my c corpse.
Eventually he did move, only for a master lich to summonstorm a bunch
of monsters onto and around the square I wanted to get to.  Broke one /
oTele to get rid of most of the monsters (luckily I was 2 squares away
from the c corpse so it didn't get thrown randomly around the level),
and zapped a second at the big h for some temporary respite.  This let
me clear a path to the c corpse, pick it up, wield it, and make
everything much easier.  If only I'd spotted my low HP at the time, I
could've invoked the staff while I had a turn's breathing space.

Despite my conducts (and general reluctance to throw elven daggers
where I might lose them, despite having 18 of the blasted things), I
only ever got mind-flayed once, and it was by Cthulhu, who also burned
my "oLS - from Vlad's tower - before I killed him, picked up the
amulet, drank the ?oGL and... gained a level.  Damnit.

Cthulhu doesn't stay dead long, so I got out of that sanctum sharpish,
and back into the fray outside.  With the help of the dead chicatrice
I was able to beat a path to the upstair and get out of there in one
piece... 'You feel like you've been here before...' had to remap my
way up to the VoTD - luckily most of the lava levels were still fresh
in my mind, so I didn't have to spend too much time in them with all
the summonstorming that was going on around me.  At some point,
Yeenoghu showed up and teamed up with an arch-lich to torment me for a
bit, but they didn't follow me up to the castle.

The rest of the way up was uneventful, until I tried to be clever and
relearn all my spells (from forgotten spellbooks, so I couldn't tell
which were important) at my stash on DL1.  Locked myself away, only
for Rodney to show up, dig a wand of digging down ontop of my book
stash, and make them all fall down somewhere I wasn't prepared to
chase after them.  Oh well, there goes that idea.  Zapped a spare poly
charge at a stack of worthless glass for the hell of it, which is
where all those citrine stones come from, dumped some stuff I wouldn't
be needing, and headed for the planes.

As it turns out, the planes were no problem, fire was first, and a
monster blundered into the portal after a few turns. After that, /oSDD
and wearing the Amulet made finding portals easy, and up at astral the
first altar was mine.

Had great fun, especially in gehennom!

